sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Gate Admin
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (eu-xx01)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/authorities
    Note over Admin,Gate: Authorization: Bearer JWT<br/>(is_admin).<br/>Body: AuthorityWrite —<br/>id, name, countryCode,<br/>subsets[]. Full schema:<br/>openapi.yaml.

    Gate->>Gate: Validate JWT (signature, exp, iss, aud),<br/>require is_admin

    Gate->>+DB: Append a new authorities row (id='aut-xxx-001', name, country_code='EE',<br/>subsets={EU07,EU01}, is_active=TRUE, created_by=admin's user-row-id).
    DB-->>-Gate: written (new row — latest row for this id wins on next read)

    Gate-->>Admin: 201 Created\n{"id":"aut-xxx-001","name":"Example Authority","countryCode":"EE","subsets":["EU07","EU01"]}

    Note over Admin: Authority registered<br/>with allowed subsets.<br/>Now create users.

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/users
    Note over Admin,Gate: Body — UserWrite:<br/>taraSub, name, email,<br/>isAdmin, isAuthority.<br/>No secret — primary<br/>auth is TARA JWT.<br/>Full schema: openapi.yaml.

    Gate->>Gate: Validate taraSub uniqueness against active users<br/>(409 if already in use)

    Gate->>+DB: Append a new users row (id=fresh UUID, tara_sub='EE00000000001',<br/>is_admin=FALSE, is_authority=TRUE, secret_hash=NULL, is_active=TRUE).
    DB-->>-Gate: written — user.id="d2e3f4a5-..."

    Gate-->>-Admin: 201 Created<br/>{"id":"d2e3f4a5-...","taraSub":"EE00000000001","name":"Example User",<br/>"isAdmin":false,"isAuthority":true,"isUserActive":true}

    Note over Admin: User auths via TARA OIDC.<br/>Gate resolves JWT `sub`<br/>to the latest active<br/>users row by tara_sub<br/>on every request.<br/>is_authority=true → may call the authority API.
